From 455213a34c75578f1b7551d57bf82f2f367c9db4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 20:01:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][VideoPlayer] Blu-ray 3D: subtitles placed by the disc
 only where it carries their sequence

The plane offsets of a Blu-ray 3D title place its subtitles in depth: a
subtitle stream follows one of up to 32 offset sequences of the second
view, named by the playlist (or, in a Matroska remux, by MakeMKV's
3d-plane tag, or guessed from the stream's place among the PGS streams).
Where the frame has no offset (after a seek, before the first group of
pictures, or for a sequence that the title does not carry at all), the
depth setting placed the subtitles.

The next commits measure the depth of a 3D video that carries none, and
must never take the place of a disc's offsets. A stream that follows a
sequence is not enough to say that the disc places it: a guessed
sequence can be one that the title does not carry, and a remux can have
lost its offsets. So:

- COffsetMetadataStore::Carries(): whether a block kept carries a
  sequence (with a test in TestBlurayOffsetMetadata);
- IRenderMsg::SubtitleDepthFromDisc(), CVideoPlayer's: the stream
  follows a sequence that the title was seen to carry. Seen once, it is
  kept while the stream follows that sequence, so that the moments the
  title says nothing about stay with the setting, as before, and the
  depth never goes from measured to the disc's and back.
---
